{
  "title": "Ingredient name resolution: names can stay pending forever; save_resolved unguarded",
  "description": "server/src/ingredient_names.rs: the table itself has good CHECKs (baseline 53-74). \
But save_resolved (689-702) updates by name with no status = pending filter and relies on the in-memory BATCH mutex (57, 475), while requeue_failed (97-113) and sync_with_catalog (291-307) run outside that lock. \
Provider-wide failures don't increment attempts (773-775), so during an outage or with a bad key a name stays pending indefinitely and the backoff lives only in memory (PROVIDER_ANSWERED, local backoff, 322-356). attempts also counts successful asks (700). \
Want: a status guard on save_resolved, and a visible persisted signal (e.g. last_error / next_attempt_at) so a stuck provider shows up somewhere instead of looking like a quiet queue. \
Found in the 2026-11-07 implicit-state-machine audit; line numbers are as of e94669d4ca, so re-check each point before fixing.",
